.TH SIMPLE_SHELL 1 "September 16, 2026" "Holberton School" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
simple_shell \- simple UNIX command interpreter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./hsh
.RB [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B simple_shell
is a simple UNIX command interpreter that executes commands entered by
the user.

The shell displays a prompt, reads a command, searches for the executable
using the PATH environment variable, and executes the command.

The shell supports both interactive and non-interactive modes.
.SH OPTIONS
This shell does not support command-line options.
.SH BUILTINS
The shell supports the following built-in commands:
.TP
.B exit
Exits the shell.
.TP
.B env
Prints the current environment.
.SH INTERACTIVE MODE
In interactive mode, the shell displays a prompt and waits for the user
to enter a command.

Example:
.PP
.nf
$ ./hsh
$ ls
$ pwd
$ exit
.fi
.SH NON-INTERACTIVE MODE
Commands can also be provided through standard input.

Example:
.PP
.nf
$ echo "ls" | ./hsh
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
Execute the shell:
.PP
.nf
$ ./hsh
.fi
.PP
Execute a command through standard input:
.PP
.nf
$ echo "/bin/ls" | ./hsh
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
The shell returns the exit status of the last command executed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The shell uses environment variables, including
.B PATH,
to locate executable commands.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sh (1),
.BR bash (1),
.BR execve (2),
.BR fork (2),
.BR wait (2)
